, one can express the SVD of 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{H}=\bm{U}^{\top}\bm{U}^{\star}$
\end_inset

 as 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{H}=\bm{X}(\cos\bm{\Theta})\bm{Y}^{\top}$
\end_inset

, where the columns of 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{X}$
\end_inset

 (resp.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $\bm{Y}$
\end_inset

) are the left (resp.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset

right) singular vectors of 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{H}$
\end_inset

, and 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{\Theta}$
\end_inset

 is a diagonal matrix composed of the principal angles between 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{U}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\bm{U}^{\star}$
\end_inset

.
 In light of this and the definition (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:defn-sgn-Z"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

), we can establish 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand eqref
reference "eq:H-sgnH-dist-general"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

 as follows 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align}
\big\|\bm{H}-\mathsf{sgn}(\bm{H})\big\| & =\big\|\bm{X}\big(\cos\bm{\Theta}-\bm{I}\big)\bm{Y}^{\top}\big\|=\big\|\bm{I}-\cos\bm{\Theta}\big\|\nonumber \\
 & =2\big\|\sin^{2}(\bm{\Theta}/2)\big\|\leq\|\sin\bm{\Theta}\|^{2}\nonumber \\
 & \leq\frac{2c_{2}^{2}\sigma^{2}n}{(\lambda_{r}^{\star})^{2}},\label{eq:H-sgnH-diff-UB-123}
\end{align}

\end_inset

where the middle line holds since 
\begin_inset Formula $1-\cos\theta=2\sin^{2}(\theta/2)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\sin(\theta/2)\leq\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\sin\theta$
\end_inset

 for any 
\begin_inset Formula $0\leq\theta\leq\pi/2$
\end_inset

, and the last line follows from 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand eqref
reference "eq:distp-U-Ustar-general"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

.
